   "text": "# How Hash Maps Handle Collisions\n\n## The Problem\n\nA hash map (dictionary) uses a **hash function** to map keys to array indices. A **collision** occurs when two different keys hash to the same index.\n\n## Common Collision Resolution Strategies\n\n| Strategy | How It Works |\n|---|---|\n| **Separate Chaining** | Each bucket holds a linked list (or other structure) of entries that hash to the same index. |\n| **Open Addressing** | If a bucket is occupied, probe for the next available slot (linear, quadratic, or double hashing). |\n\nPython's `dict` uses **open addressing** with **linear probing** (and some optimizations).\n\n## Python Example: Separate Chaining (Manual Implementation)\n\n```python\nclass HashMap:\n    def __init__(self, size=16):\n        self.size = size\n        # Each bucket is a list of (key, value) pairs",
